Task #966: Add RSS/Atom feeds so SEO score reaches 100

The validator (vite-plugin-seo-validate.ts) checks for 6 feed files:
feed.xml, feed/cities.xml, feed/services.xml, feed/atom.xml,
feed/cities-atom.xml, feed/services-atom.xml. The feedsPlugin already
existed and was wired into vite.config.ts, but only listed cities and
services — content hub coverage was missing per the task spec.

Changes
- vite-plugin-feeds.ts: extended the global RSS + Atom feed to include
  per-city content hub entries (/guide/<city> and
  /best/<service>/in/<city> using BUILD_SERVICE_CATEGORIES[0]) for the
  first 15 phase-1 cities. URLs match the real prerender routes in
  vite-plugin-prerender.ts (verified against /best/:service/in/:city).
  Timestamps use CONTENT_LASTMOD.guides / CONTENT_LASTMOD.best.
- Updated the [feeds] log line to report item counts per feed for build
  visibility.

Verification
- Ran the plugin standalone via tsx; all 6 expected files were written
  to dist/ (feed.xml ~27KB / 70 items, feed/cities.xml ~25KB / 53 items,
  feed/services.xml ~25KB / 67 items, plus 3 Atom variants).
- Validator's missing-feeds check will now report 0 missing feeds, so
  the 10-point feeds component of the SEO score is fully earned.

No deviations from the task scope. Did not run a full vite build (it
exceeds the 2-minute tool timeout in this env); the plugin is exercised
by the same code path on every production build.

